ndicated in at least six distinct patient groups: QT间隔延长患者, 低血钾患者, 有家族性猝死史患者, 有心脏病史患者, 肝肾功能不良者, and 脉率缓慢患者 [Data: Relationships (6134, 6135, 6137, 6138, 6139, 6140)]. These contraindications reflect the class’s proarrhythmic potential and metabolic burden on the liver and kidneys. The evidence consistently notes that electrolyte imbalances (e.g., hypokalemia) and pre-existing cardiac conduction abnormalities significantly amplify the risk of torsades de pointes and sudden cardiac death when macrolides are administered [Data: Relationships (10887, 6135)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug–drug interactions mediated by CYP3A4 inhibition\",\n            \"explanation\": \"A key mechanism underlying many macrolide-related risks is their inhibition of the CYP3A4 hepatic enzyme. First-generation macrolides like 红霉素 and 三乙酞竹桃霉素 strongly inhibit CYP3A4, forming stable complexes that impair metabolism of co-administered drugs such as 特非那丁, leading to dangerous accumulation [Data: Relationships (43634)]. In contrast, newer agents like 氟红霉素 and 克拉红霉素 exhibit moderate binding, while 阿奇霉素 shows minimal interaction [Data: Relationships (57580, 55696)]. Clinicians are advised to monitor blood levels of drugs like 卡马西平 when co-prescribed with certain macrolides, as their concentrations can rise significantly [Data: Relationships (1671)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Dermatological and mucosal adverse effects are documented\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond systemic toxicity, macrolides are associated with localized adverse effects such as 药疹 and 会阴糜烂. 药疹 is specifically linked to 乙酰螺旋霉素 [Data: Relationships (8425)], while 会阴糜烂—though rare—is also attributed to the same drug based on case reports involving high-dose regimens [Data: Relationships (8424)]. These reactions typically emerge 1–2 weeks after initiation and may be reversible upon discontinuation. Although less life-threatening than cardiac or hepatic effects, they con